{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"afb4ac9d0d48128819e093f298993f2c9a336a69e7ad2a5d49b10a48e4d53ba2","packTokens":2766,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":273,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":616,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1556,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement PO and receiving data, map PO lines to lots and pens, and forecast lifecycle targets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, forecasts, wastage, ration recipes, and ration costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Create pen-level feeding plans and log feeding activities, updating inventory and lot consumption and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements and maintain weight histories.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics and predictive sale/feeding insights, updating when feeding or weight events are recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational dashboards, reports, filters, CSV/PDF exports, and yard-level summaries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Create mock data and present the proposed solution, architecture, demo, testing, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What user access model is required for operational and financial records?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one shared access level for all users; do not distinguish permissions by role.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how must a feeding plan allocate its planned quantity?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require a quantity allocation to each lot and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the plan.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the configured wastage ratio affect inventory decrements for an actual feeding event?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Decrement stock by the actual delivered quantity and apply wastage only to estimated consumption and forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How should total lot weight be handled when a user records average weight and the number of animals weighed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate total measured weight as average weight multiplied by the number weighed; do not accept a conflicting independent total.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What cost basis should the lot-level profitability analysis include?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Show feed cost per unit of weight gain using recorded feed costs only.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in, given that all users have the same access level?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No sign-in; anyone with the app link can access the shared workspace.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"When a pen contains multiple lots, how should an actual feeding quantity be attributed to those lots for lot-level consumption and cost metrics?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allocate the actual quantity to lots in proportion to their planned quantities.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which ingredient cost should be used to calculate the cost of a saved feeding event when the ingredient's unit cost changes over time?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the ingredient unit cost recorded when the feeding event is saved.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a shared Feedlot web workspace through an app link without sign-in or role-specific controls, with the same operational and financial controls for all users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Add mock procurement synchronization that requests and displays PO and receiving details, and map PO lines to one or more lots and pens with traceability, pen capacity, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Display import duplicates, changed or conflicting records, returned conflict status and mappings, and a review action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Show lot lifecycle targets and projected market or ship dates, applying lot-specific targets when available and the configured yard target otherwise, displaying the yard target for all lots, and leaving projected dates empty when ADG is zero or negative.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Add feed inventory entry and viewing with item details and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock; when a movement is refused for insufficient stock, show the returned shortage and error while keeping the unsaved movement available for correction.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let users configure wastage and view returned ingredient balances and shortages across daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons, marking periods without a dated feeding plan as unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let users create, save, view, and compare rations, including ingredients or as-fed proportions, nutrition, intended animal type or weight range, returned cost per pound, and associated lot performance or cost-of-gain values; identify the lowest returned cost of gain when available.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"For ton-denominated inventory or ration prices, show the equivalent per-pound price in the configured currency and display calculation quantities in pounds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let users generate dated pen feeding plans from a ration, per-animal daily rate, animal count, and feeding time, and display returned quantities, feed cost, energy intake, and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"For multi-lot pens, require a planned quantity allocation for every lot and flag missing or unreconciled allocations; show the single-lot allocation field for pens with one lot.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"On saved feeding-event details, show returned planned and actual quantities, variance, feed cost, energy, inventory decrement based on delivered quantity, feeding status, lot allocations, and ingredient unit-cost snapshot; show wastage-adjusted estimated consumption separately when applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show planned-versus-actual feeding variance and provide an action to adjust a future plan, with editable quantity fields and the selected pen and ration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Let users record dated lot weight measurements with number weighed, average weight, and notes; calculate total measured weight from average weight and number weighed, with no independently editable total-weight field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Show lot weight history as a time-ordered list with returned dates, average and total weight, number weighed, gain since the prior measurement, and notes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"When saved feeding or weight records are edited or voided, show returned revised balances and metrics while retaining the original record in history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned creator and last-changed identifiers and timestamps on record details without presenting a full audit log.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned lot feed-to-gain metrics, including days on feed, weight gain, ADG, feed consumed, FCR, feed cost per unit of gain, and projected ship date; calculate feed cost per unit of gain using recorded feed costs only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"After feeding or weight events are saved, refresh returned lot metrics and show returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an operational dashboard with active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned and actual feed, feed consumed and cost, weights and gains, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, cost per gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Provide operational reports showing the highest-consuming pen, best feed-to-gain lot, highest-ADG lot, most-used ration, feeding alignment, overfed or underfed pens, remaining inventory, and cost per gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a Feed-to-Gain report with date-range, lot, breed, sex, and pen filters to compare returned ADG, FCR, and cost of gain across matching lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Allow the filtered Feed-to-Gain report results and selected scope to be exported as CSV and PDF.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a yard-level summary of aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Provide representative mock operational data and a project presentation page covering the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo walkthrough, coding prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market strategy and analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Render every page responsively for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}